1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:08,049
A movie director is making a film
on the Tenpo famine,

2
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:10,010
and they want to film
a peasant eating grass.

3
00:00:10,093 --> 00:00:11,219
A period movie!

4
00:00:11,302 --> 00:00:13,096
Konta, congratulations!

5
00:00:13,179 --> 00:00:15,974
-Congratulations!
-Konta! Congratulations!

6
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:18,226
<i>Obon </i>holidays, huh.

7
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:22,439
Shouldn't we at least visit Midori's
grandma's grave? She built this villa.

8
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:24,607
-Grandma's photo!
-I want to see it!

9
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:26,776
She was a beauty.

10
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:28,194
I found a <i>yukata </i>in the storage room.

11
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:30,155
Try it on.
Must be a keepsake from your grandma.

12
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:34,617
-Ta-da!
-Oh! So cute!

13
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:35,952
Summer festival?

14
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:37,537
<i>Shall I guide you?</i>

15
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:38,872
Wow.

16
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:40,832
Could this be…

17
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:41,833
My Grandma's?

18
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:44,627
Ms. Nobuko really loved this town.

19
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:45,920
Can I take this back with me?

20
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:46,838
It's <i>Obon</i>, after all.

21
00:00:46,921 --> 00:00:50,383
I think Grandma would be happier
if we kept them in the villa.

22
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:53,845
<i>This way</i>
<i>Grandma can return to the villa too.</i>

23
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:56,806
I'm glad I met you, Mr. Nishigami.

24
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:01,603
<i>I'm home, Mr. Nishigami.</i>

25
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:11,154
-So hot! Sorry Grandma!
-Hey, careful!

26
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:21,289
Grandma, welcome back.

27
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:25,877
Grandma, I think it's about time
I find success.

28
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:27,712
So help me out!

29
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:29,839
Make<i> The Great Tenpo Famine </i>a hit!

30
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:32,091
Grandma, nice to meet you.

31
00:01:32,175 --> 00:01:34,761
I'm Rinrin,
Midori's classmate from university.

32
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:38,348
I have been feeling
very refreshed at your villa.

33
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:41,309
Man, it really is a nice villa.

34
00:01:41,392 --> 00:01:45,104
I got to enjoy my vacation
while chipping away at my savings.

35
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:48,108
We caught rainbow trout and ate them.

36
00:01:48,191 --> 00:01:50,318
Sorry for taking life from this land.

37
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:55,907
Grandma,
thank you for leaving this villa behind.

38
00:01:56,449 --> 00:02:01,037
I lost my job, but thanks to this villa,

39
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:03,456
I can have fun like this now.

40
00:02:04,791 --> 00:02:08,419
I think we siblings made you
worry a lot, but from now on,

41
00:02:08,503 --> 00:02:12,882
I will find my path
and move forward with all I have.

42
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:17,053
-All right, let's eat.
-Yeah.

43
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:18,847
Let's make an offering to Grandma too.

44
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:20,431
-All right, let's drink!
-Yeah!

45
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:22,767
-I'll make some stupid alcohol for her.
-What?

46
00:02:23,726 --> 00:02:25,186
-It's fine.
-Regular alcohol is fine.

47
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:27,188
I think she would like my alcohol!

48
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:29,899
No, that gives you a hangover.

49
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:31,401
Do you want some, Grandma?

50
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:35,738
It has been a while,

51
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:37,031
Mr. Nishigami.

52
00:02:38,783 --> 00:02:41,452
Why are you here?

53
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:47,625
At the end of summer,
a great flood will come,

54
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:50,670
and there will be a landslide.

55
00:02:52,714 --> 00:02:53,882
Oh, dear!

56
00:02:55,216 --> 00:02:57,886
So, will they all die?

57
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:01,431
They're still so young!

58
00:03:02,015 --> 00:03:05,476
They haven't gotten
to live their lives yet, unlike me!

59
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:08,062
There is nothing I can do.

60
00:03:10,106 --> 00:03:11,149
Please!

61
00:03:11,232 --> 00:03:13,151
Can't you save them?

62
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:16,821
That is a grave violation of the rules.

63
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:22,827
If you break the rules,
what will happen to you?

64
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:29,000
It is impossible
for a Grim Reaper to break the rules.

65
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:31,961
Goodness…

66
00:03:33,254 --> 00:03:34,213
Hey.

67
00:03:34,923 --> 00:03:39,636
If I try to change their destiny,

68
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:43,139
will you be violating the rules
for telling me this?

69
00:03:45,391 --> 00:03:46,351
I don't know.

70
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:50,313
There is no precedent.

71
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:38,945
Hey, Midori.

72
00:04:39,028 --> 00:04:41,406
How was it with Mr. Nishigami?

73
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:44,242
You've been acting weird
since you came back.

74
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:46,452
Could it be you two kissed?

75
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:48,413
-No way!
-What are you talking about?

76
00:04:48,496 --> 00:04:49,956
We didn't!

77
00:04:50,039 --> 00:04:52,542
Then did you hold hands?

78
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:53,793
-Huh?
-What?

79
00:04:53,876 --> 00:04:54,961
-Really?
-Who knows.

80
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:56,629
Hey, you girls.

81
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:58,631
This is no time to fool around.

82
00:04:59,215 --> 00:05:01,592
You all must leave this place.

83
00:05:01,676 --> 00:05:03,886
You'll die in the typhoon!

84
00:05:05,179 --> 00:05:06,597
Did you really hold hands?

85
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:07,640
No.

86
00:05:07,724 --> 00:05:09,225
Not exactly, but…

87
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:11,436
But the vibes were good, right?

88
00:05:12,478 --> 00:05:13,896
What should I do?

89
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,773
They can't hear me.

90
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:17,483
Someone help!

91
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:21,362
Please deliver my voice to these children!

92
00:05:21,863 --> 00:05:23,698
<i>Yes, I can hear you.</i>

93
00:05:25,658 --> 00:05:26,993
-Huh?
-What?

94
00:05:27,618 --> 00:05:28,661
Did it say something?

95
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:30,163
Wait.

96
00:05:30,246 --> 00:05:31,497
What is this?

97
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:32,415
Hey.

98
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:34,876
Hey, help me!

99
00:05:34,959 --> 00:05:36,085
<i>Yes!</i>

100
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:38,212
<i>What kind of help do you need?</i>

101
00:05:38,296 --> 00:05:41,132
-The AI activated on its own?
-I wonder why?

102
00:05:41,215 --> 00:05:43,259
Tell my grandchildren for me.

103
00:05:44,177 --> 00:05:46,512
<i>A message for your grandchildren?</i>

104
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:48,139
-Yes!
-Grandchildren?

105
00:05:48,222 --> 00:05:49,766
We didn't say anything, though.

106
00:05:49,849 --> 00:05:51,559
-It must be broken.
<i>-Understood.</i>

107
00:05:51,642 --> 00:05:55,188
<i>I can repeat the sentences you say.</i>

108
00:05:55,271 --> 00:05:58,232
<i>What do you want me to repeat?</i>

109
00:05:59,859 --> 00:06:03,404
You are all grown adults,
yet you don't even work.

110
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:04,822
You stay here every day,

111
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:07,742
drinking alcohol,
just idling around in a place like this!

112
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:11,788
<i>You are all grown adults, yet you</i>
<i>don't even work, you stay here every day,</i>

113
00:06:11,871 --> 00:06:14,123
<i>drinking alcohol, just idling around…</i>

114
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:17,001
-Why does it know about our lives?
-So weird.

115
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:18,419
In the first place,

116
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:25,384
this villa isn't a place
for young people like you to come!

117
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:28,596
<i>In the first place, a villa like this</i>

118
00:06:28,679 --> 00:06:32,225
<i>isn't a place</i>
<i>for young people like you to come!</i>

119
00:06:32,308 --> 00:06:37,396
This is a place for people who have
achieved a certain amount of success,

120
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:41,484
and are semi-retired, to come to relax!

121
00:06:41,567 --> 00:06:44,195
<i>This is a place for people who have</i>

122
00:06:44,278 --> 00:06:49,492
<i>achieved a certain amount of success,</i>
<i>and are semi-retired, to come to relax!</i>

123
00:06:49,575 --> 00:06:52,620
We want to succeed, but we can't!

124
00:06:52,703 --> 00:06:55,623
It will be okay!
You have<i> The Great Tenpo Famine </i>coming up!

125
00:06:55,706 --> 00:07:00,002
Go back to Tokyo right now!

126
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:03,005
<i>Go back to Tokyo right now.</i>

127
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:05,383
We won't go back now!

128
00:07:05,466 --> 00:07:07,051
We're on vacation!

129
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:08,511
Wow, so strict.

130
00:07:08,594 --> 00:07:12,682
I see, then I need a different approach.

131
00:07:13,182 --> 00:07:15,810
<i>I see, then I need a different approach.</i>

132
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:17,395
What did it say?

133
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:21,232
This villa

134
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:24,026
is cursed!

135
00:07:24,735 --> 00:07:26,195
If you stay here,

136
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:31,033
all of you will die!

137
00:07:31,617 --> 00:07:34,162
<i>This villa is cursed.</i>

138
00:07:34,245 --> 00:07:37,415
<i>If you stay here, all of you will die!</i>

139
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:41,252
Because, at the end of summer…

140
00:07:41,335 --> 00:07:43,796
<i>Because, at the end of summer…</i>

141
00:07:44,338 --> 00:07:46,799
-What?
-A blackout?

142
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:48,926
Did the breaker trip?

143
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:50,845
Konta, go check the breaker.

144
00:07:50,928 --> 00:07:52,054
What is a breaker?

145
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:53,431
-What?
-And where is it?

146
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:57,143
I don't know, maybe over there?
In the hallway? Go look for it!

147
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:58,519
I'm going.

148
00:07:58,603 --> 00:07:59,562
Well, it's fine.

149
00:07:59,645 --> 00:08:02,982
Let's just make
a bonfire out there and drink.

150
00:08:03,065 --> 00:08:06,152
No way! I'm scared when it's so dark!

151
00:08:06,235 --> 00:08:09,113
-Konta, where are you? Come back!
-What's wrong, Rinrin?

152
00:08:09,197 --> 00:08:10,990
I'll look for a flashlight.

153
00:08:11,073 --> 00:08:12,158
-Hey!
-A flashlight?

154
00:08:12,241 --> 00:08:13,659
-Oh.
-Right.

155
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:17,538
What's wrong?

156
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:19,624
-You okay?
-What?

157
00:08:19,707 --> 00:08:21,918
I thought I saw your grandma's face.

158
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:23,711
Hey, cut it out. Why say that?

159
00:08:23,794 --> 00:08:25,880
It looked like your grandma, Midori.

160
00:08:25,963 --> 00:08:28,299
-What?
-Just like the photo.

161
00:08:28,382 --> 00:08:32,053
-Cut it out, I'm scared!
-It's scary, isn't it?

162
00:08:33,387 --> 00:08:34,639
Oh, it's <i>Obon</i>!

163
00:08:34,722 --> 00:08:36,641
Grandma came to visit us!

164
00:08:40,811 --> 00:08:43,064
Grandma!

165
00:08:43,981 --> 00:08:44,899
Hey!

166
00:08:44,982 --> 00:08:47,318
Grandma, can you hear me?

167
00:08:47,401 --> 00:08:49,403
It's me, Midori.

168
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:53,115
Grandma, you know,

169
00:08:54,033 --> 00:08:57,119
since coming to this villa,
I've been so happy.

170
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:59,664
I've been enjoying the summer oranges
from the garden.

171
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:01,249
I make them into juice!

172
00:09:01,332 --> 00:09:03,000
Mixed with alcohol, though.

173
00:09:03,084 --> 00:09:08,047
Grandma, this villa is dear to you,
so I will take care of it forever!

174
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:10,424
Mr. Nishigami is here too, so it's fine.

175
00:09:11,008 --> 00:09:14,303
Next year, the year after next,
even when I become an adult…

176
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:15,680
You are an adult, though.

177
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:19,016
Even when I become a granny,
forever and ever.

178
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:22,770
So that we can all spend
our vacations at this villa together.

179
00:09:50,214 --> 00:09:51,299
-Huh?
-What the heck?

180
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:59,015
What are you two doing?

181
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:08,024
I think what I did backfired.

182
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:13,321
I thought if I pretended to be a ghost,
they would be scared and stay away.

183
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:16,824
But they…

184
00:10:16,907 --> 00:10:18,576
They know what I look like?

185
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:20,870
It's <i>Obon</i>.

186
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:26,876
They found old photos of you
and put them up around the house.

187
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:27,960
So…

188
00:10:28,544 --> 00:10:29,545
I see.

189
00:10:31,255 --> 00:10:33,132
That recognized me.

190
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:40,097
You didn't mention the landslide, did you?

191
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:41,724
I did!

192
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:43,267
I said it,

193
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:47,104
but that machine
didn't pick up those words.

194
00:10:47,688 --> 00:10:48,814
I see.

195
00:10:50,941 --> 00:10:53,361
Perhaps Lady Yomi intervened.

196
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:54,779
Hey.

197
00:10:54,862 --> 00:10:56,530
Please, Mr. Nishigami.

198
00:10:56,614 --> 00:10:58,491
Save those children.

199
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,410
They are still so young.

200
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:05,623
And they have to die just because
they came here? It's a tragedy!

201
00:11:05,706 --> 00:11:09,126
When I meet them in heaven,
how do I even apologize…

202
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:12,296
I cannot do as you requested.

203
00:11:13,964 --> 00:11:14,840
Wait.

204
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:16,801
Please, Mr. Nishigami. Please.

205
00:11:16,884 --> 00:11:19,470
Let me talk with them!

206
00:11:20,137 --> 00:11:21,806
I cannot do that.

207
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:51,544
<i>I am relieved, Grim Reaper.</i>

208
00:11:52,503 --> 00:11:56,841
<i>Lately, you have been playing around</i>
<i>with those humans almost every day,</i>

209
00:11:56,924 --> 00:11:58,509
<i>so I was worried.</i>

210
00:11:59,176 --> 00:12:02,847
<i>But it seems you understand</i>
<i>what your duties are.</i>

211
00:12:04,473 --> 00:12:05,683
Yes…

212
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:10,354
<i>That old woman</i>
<i>lived out her natural lifespan,</i>

213
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:13,482
<i>so she was able to come back for </i>Obon<i>.</i>

214
00:12:14,066 --> 00:12:15,901
<i>The lives of humans</i>

215
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:20,406
<i>are built around comforting</i>
<i>the dead at every opportunity.</i>

216
00:12:23,993 --> 00:12:26,620
To comfort the dead…

217
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:29,915
<i>Only in death is a human complete.</i>

218
00:12:30,499 --> 00:12:34,420
<i>With death, their lives are fulfilled.</i>

219
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:09,914
Grandma…

220
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:14,335
Thanks to you,

221
00:13:15,336 --> 00:13:16,337
I may…

222
00:13:19,089 --> 00:13:22,009
be falling in love for the first time!

223
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:29,517
<i>As the </i>Obon <i>holiday comes to an end,</i>

224
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:33,354
<i>people are rushing back</i>
<i>from hometowns and tourist destinations.</i>

225
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,272
<i>On expressways,</i>

226
00:13:35,356 --> 00:13:39,610
<i>heavy congestion has been occurring</i>
<i>since morning, mainly on inbound lines,</i>

227
00:13:39,693 --> 00:13:44,031
<i>with long lines of cars</i>
<i>even exceeding 30 to 40 kilometers.</i>

228
00:13:46,283 --> 00:13:48,118
HATO SABLÉS!

229
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:18,899
This person…

230
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:22,111
Who is this?

231
00:14:36,834 --> 00:14:38,002
Thank you.

232
00:14:43,841 --> 00:14:45,009
<i>Now to our next story.</i>

233
00:14:45,759 --> 00:14:47,761
<i>From now until the end of summer,</i>

234
00:14:47,845 --> 00:14:52,016
<i>there will be increased risk</i>
<i>of powerful typhoons forming.</i>

235
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,226
<i>According to the Meteorological Agency…</i>

236
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:30,429
<i>Orange peels…</i>

237
00:15:30,512 --> 00:15:32,056
<i>How do you make them?</i>

238
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:33,807
<i>If you want, we can make them together.</i>

239
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:35,476
Konta. I'm going with you.

240
00:15:35,559 --> 00:15:36,435
Tetsuro!

241
00:15:36,518 --> 00:15:38,145
I'm going to fish for horse mackerel.

242
00:15:38,228 --> 00:15:40,230
You got the first fish!

243
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:44,610
In order to survive,
you even have to eat grass!

244
00:15:44,693 --> 00:15:46,528
You're interested in Midori, aren't you?

245
00:15:47,237 --> 00:15:49,031
<i>Am I?</i>

246
00:15:49,114 --> 00:15:50,491
<i>Hey, so…</i>

247
00:15:50,574 --> 00:15:53,202
What is our relationship right now?

248
00:15:53,285 --> 00:15:56,246
<i>Your recent actions</i>
<i>have been unacceptable.</i>

249
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:59,500
<i>Falling in love with a human</i>
<i>is out of the question.</i>

250
00:15:59,583 --> 00:16:03,671
